# From the post of 2022-01-23 (studies/data/notes/post-no-limbo-no-purgatory.html), in the author's words.

=== No limbo
--- No limbo and no purgatory [title]
overline: A post from the channel
heading: No limbo and no purgatory
sub: There's no righteousness outside that imputed to the saved from believing on Christ.
hint: Use the arrow keys or swipe to move through the slides. Tap any gold reference to read the verse.

--- No limbo
lead: I don't know who needs to hear this but no, Jesus did not "go to limbo and free the souls of the just" like Plato and Virgil, "trapped there because they didn't know who Jesus was."
p: There are no 'just' without calling upon the name of the Lord. There's no righteousness outside that imputed to the saved from believing on Christ.

--- None righteous
big: Romans 3:10

=== Hell and Heaven
--- Hell and Heaven [title]
heading: Hell and Heaven
lead: There is no Limbo or "Purgatory." There is Hell and Heaven.
take: [[Luke 16:22|"Abraham's bosom"]] is literally his chest when he hugs and comforts another spirit coming home to God, in Heaven.
